/* rete#226 — THE ONE COPY OF THE PRIMITIVE SELECTOR LIST.

   Read by TWO consumers that must never disagree: dispatch.c builds PRIM_NAMES from it
   (index i -> prim id i+1, the enum's own convention), and the image builders bake each
   Symbol's prim id from it (nsl/tools/solidify.py for Model A, oimg_serialize.py for
   Model B). Before this file the list lived only in C, so baking ids at image build would
   have meant a SECOND copy in Python — and the C side already carries a compile-time
   parity guard against the enum precisely because a list that drifts misroutes every prim
   after the insertion point, silently.

   APPEND-ONLY, and the order IS the id. Never reorder, never delete: a prim id is a
   number baked into every image built before the edit. Adding one means appending here
   and advancing dispatch.c's prim_names_enum_parity_check to the new last enum member.

   One name per line, no trailing commas — the Python readers split on the quotes. */
PRIM_NAME("Array")
PRIM_NAME("new:")
